From 2772c7ededf96f05aca9a18bc4753c3dbdea30e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 03:59:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] perf(lighting): propagate increased block light incrementally

Flood-fill new emission into cached light arrays and send only changed sections. Recompute the versioned region when emission falls, opacity changes, or nearby chunk state is incomplete; align light snapshots with waterlogged Java block states.

Resolve Bedrock slab filtering by Java slab type when constructing the
light snapshot table. An isolated official Bedrock Dedicated Server
1.26.51.1 probe, build 51061372 and protocol 2193, measured getSkyLightLevel
and getLightLevel through sealed shafts and tunnels without client joins.
Top and bottom oak and smooth-stone slabs read skylight 14 at the slab
then 13 below; double slabs block both sky and block light. Java combines
half and double slabs under one identifier, so its identifier opacity
zero loses both native distinctions. Half slabs now filter one level
and type=double filters 15.

The same target probe shows top/bottom stairs pass full skylight 15,
water and leaves filter one level, and single slabs pass block light
14 then 13. Preserve those measured scalar rules instead of importing
Java face occlusion. Numeric propagation tests reproduce the native
shaft and tunnel measurements; raw official probe output stays private.
